 "result": "Look at `locate_main_app` (`src/tessel/cli.py:41`), specifically the factory-fallback loop at lines 66–85.\n\n- **Why it fails:** the loop finds `create_app` but calls it with no arguments (`app_factory()` at line 72). Your required `config_name` raises a `TypeError`.\n- **`_bad_factory_args` (line 94):** it inspects the traceback to tell whether the `TypeError` came from the call itself (bad arguments) or from inside the factory. Here the call itself failed, so it returns `True`. That produces the `NoAppException` at lines 80–85: \"could not call it without arguments\".\n- **Fix:** no code change is needed. The message tells you to pass the argument explicitly, e.g. `tessel run --app 'yourmodule:create_app(\"dev\")'`. That path goes through `find_app_by_string` (line 120), which parses the call and its arguments.\n- **Alternative:** give `config_name` a default, or expose a module-level `app`, so auto-discovery works.",
